For $mu in cal(M)$, let $z_1 = mu(0)$, $z_2 = mu(1)$, and $z_3 = mu(oo)$. Compose a transformation of the form $gamma compose beta_b$ to send $z_3$ to $oo$, then a translation to send the image of $z_1$ to $0$, and finally a scaling to send the image of $z_2$ to $1$. The resulting transformation sends $(z_1,z_2,z_3)$ to $(0,1,oo)$, so the three-point lemma shows it is $mu^(-1)$. Thus $mu$ is a product of the three stated types and their inverses.
